            <div xml:id="d976">

                <pb facs="1472" n="1458" xml:id="pg1458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 LCC/13: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-27T20:00:00+01:00">January 27, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 27—5:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>729. At a meeting of the American members of the London Political Warfare
                    Coordinating Committee today there was some discussion of the Department’s 378,
                    January 14, midnight, the substance of which has been communicated to Sir Orme
                    Sargent. There developed some doubt as to whether the Department’s reference to
                    the drafting of joint Anglo, American, Russian political warfare plans subject
                    to higher authority means that the enlarged Committee will take part in the
                    preparation of weekly propaganda directives or whether they will from time to
                    time meet to evolve an over-all propaganda policy plan which will remain in
                    effect if approved by higher authority until changed by the Committee and which
                    will be binding upon OWI, PWE and the appropriate Russian agencies in the
                    preparation of the weekly directives. The Department’s views on this point as
                    soon as possible will be appreciated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
